          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.11,
            0.883,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is the three-dimensional (3D) equivalent of a circle. Whereas a circle is the collection of all points "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in a plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that are at some given distance from some given point, a sphere is the collection of all points in 3D space that are at some given distance r (the radius of the sphere) from a given point O, the centre of the sphere. If we rotate the circle about any diameter, we obtain a hollow sphere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.24,
            0.875,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.158,
                0.24,
                0.875,
                0.441
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.45,
            0.884,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Archimedes showed that the surface area A of a sphere with radius r is equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\pi r ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . He did this by showing that the surface area of a sphere is exactly equal to the curved surface area of a cylinder with radius r and height h = 2r that fits tightly over the sphere, Fig. 14.12."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.536,
            0.607,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.301,
                0.536,
                0.607,
                0.718
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.451,
                0.721,
                0.549,
                0.74
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 14.12"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.754,
            0.729,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The curved surface area of such a cylinder is equal to"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.378,
            0.779,
            0.62,
            0.799
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "2\\pi r h = 2\\pi r \\times 2r = 4\\pi r^{2},"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.809,
            0.633,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is the formula obtained by Archimedes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
